            <ArticleTitle>Headache in women.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>417-28, viii</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Women have more migraine than men. Some secondary headaches are more common in women. Menses, pregnancy, and menopause have an impact on the frequency and treatment of headache. Oral contraceptives can be used in women with migraine with some precautions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
